<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Spring bids mixed.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Spring bids mixed.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring wheat bids were mixed on Thursday amid a continued pickup in farm sales sparked by recent gains in wheat futures, several dealers said.</p>
<p>Wheat futures on all three exchanges, KCBT, CBOT and MGE, were up, drawing support from higher CBOT soybeans and soymeal. March MGE futures gained 2-3/4 cents to end at $3.94-1/4 a bushel.</p>
<p>&quot;People are hauling grain due to the recent rally,&quot; a North Dakota dealer said. Another Montana dealer said he saw more spring than winter wheat moving.  </p>
